From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:32:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(open-items): tell agents with the tools to raise and
 close items with them

Agents follow the item-label instruction, which has them pick label
numbers themselves and close an item only by striking it in chat. With
the open items tools available, that would leave the store unused, the
numbers made up and the chat text deciding what is open.

Agents whose spec keeps the open_items tool group get one shorter block
in its place: raise first (several per call, each with a topic), write
each item once in chat with the returned label and a bold title, refer
to it by label afterwards and never write a label the tool did not
return; answer comments on items ("Comments on N items:") with
sys_open_items_update replies, closing with a one-line resolution only
what that settles; leave items the user closed ("(closed by me)") closed
unless asked again; list instead of relying on memory. It never asks for
struck labels, so nothing written in chat changes an item. SDK harnesses
get it every turn in place of the item-label instruction; native
harnesses get it at launch, swapped in for the item-label paragraph
(build_native_startup_instructions is wrapped rather than edited, so
guidance other changes add to its list composes with it). The runner
drops the group when the server does not store open items, so those
sessions, and launches without a spec, keep the text-label instruction.

Not proposed upstream yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
